The waves grow, their gentle caress on my weathered skin,
A delicate balance of life and death's cruel hand;
As I float among its depths, my soul is bathed in an omen so grand that it seems to stretch out before me like a sea serpent.

I feel the salty air fill my lungs, as if the ocean itself was exhaling a sigh of relief;
The waves rise and fall in perfect harmony on this dark shore,
A symphony of life's fury, where every moment is a battleground.

In this vast expanse, I am but a vessel, carrying the sea to its destination, no matter how small it may seem;
For in its beauty, there lies a secret that has been hidden for so long:
The ocean's mysteries, like whispers of forgotten memories,
A reminder that even in death we are part.

